  "id": "COMPOUND:2734 - PROTEIN:6293",
  "verbalization": "Stanolone is proposed to interact with Dipeptidyl peptidase IX through multiple distinct pathways, each involving different targets. The first pathway links Stanolone to Liver X receptor (LXR alpha and beta), which is subsequently targeted by Hydroxysaikosaponin c, and this cascade ultimately affects Dipeptidyl peptidase IX. The second and third pathways connect Stanolone to 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase, which is targeted by two different compounds, both of which also target Dipeptidyl peptidase IX. These findings suggest that Stanolone may modulate Dipeptidyl peptidase IX through diverse mechanisms involving nuclear receptors and enzymatic pathways. The evidence supports a potential role for Stanolone in influencing Dipeptidyl peptidase IX activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with each step contributing to a broader regulatory network that may underlie the drug's effects.",
